{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "29", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "15", "M": "52", "S": "52"}}, "news": [{"title": "Kolhapur civic body to regularise pre-2011 residential encroachments", "para": "Kolhapur municipal corporation will regularize residential encroachments made before 2011. Plots up to 500 square feet will be regularized free of cost. Online applications will be accepted from September 7, with special camps. Plots exceeding 1,500 square feet and those on riverbeds are ineligible. Charges will apply for plots between 500 and 1,500 square feet.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/kolhapur-civic-body-to-regularise-pre-2011-residential-encroachments/133612008?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-270632/133612008.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Himachal Pardesh HC expresses concern over illegal multi-storey buildings in Solan hills", "para": "The Himachal Pradesh High Court has raised alarms over unauthorized constructions that threaten the region's ecology. In a call to action, the court has requested comprehensive details from the government regarding these developments. Images reveal significant building activities leading to a stark decline in greenery between 2015 and 2026. The hearing will continue on September 15.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/himachal-pardesh-hc-expresses-concern-over-illegal-multi-storey-buildings-in-solan-hills/133611958?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-243912/133611958.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Greater Noida authority raises farmers\u2019 land aid by \u20b92,200 per sq meter ahead of phase-II acquisition", "para": "The Greater Noida Authority recently announced an increase in farmer compensation to Rs 6,415 per square meter. For farmers selecting abadi plots, the compensation is pegged at Rs 5,725 per square meter. This adjustment is designed to facilitate land acquisition for the second phase, covering approximately 40,000 hectares across 140 villages, and is a step towards resolving previous protests from farmers.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/greater-noida-authority-raises-farmers-land-aid-by-2200-per-sq-meter-ahead-of-phase-ii-acquisition/133611937?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-151554/133611937.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}